{"id":"39d0e38b-d127-4d44-8458-21e01bd74d52","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"013db6950c147f6a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/code-refactor.ts","baseline":{"blob":"69dd23790e245056fc35f4bd476e7c0e3f3306d5","start":1575,"end":1594},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","TRY_MS","=","1000"]},"context":{"before":"b98e97d518781919","after":"a8934920692ccaa5"}},"payload":{"text":"How far apart a move's edits are asked for while TypeScript isn't answering or doesn't hold the file yet (a workspace just\nopened, its server still starting), and for how long before it's said that they couldn't be worked out.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:17:38.052Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:17:38.052Z"}
{"id":"5e6907c3-debb-4364-b018-a99c592a91b7","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"0c75a4a4aed60513","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/code-refactor.ts","baseline":{"blob":"4d29b8b5001b72a13a09968fb438ab5d2c087fd2","start":3177,"end":3238},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","following","=","new","Map","<","string",",","Promise","<","vscodeApi",".","Uri","[]",">",">","(",")"]},"context":{"before":"f53fc1de5443133a","after":"e2f925c8d3ef1eab"}},"payload":{"text":"Each move's import edits under way, by the move (`from to`): what `code.move` waits on and saves.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:17:30.772Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:17:30.772Z"}
{"id":"7e1a2d28-da91-429a-a7a4-9fe287e0e6bb","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a4eb2d27eddc588a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/code-refactor.ts","baseline":{"blob":"274b050a24051a89a94c46b522bbe2119b8df50e","start":0,"end":46},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Hub","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/hub","\""]},"context":{"after":"e44371a09dbded9a"}},"payload":{"text":"Refactoring, as the editor does it (Refactoring for agents). A file moved or renamed in the Explorer keeps its imports right:\nevery import of it, and its own relative ones, changed as TypeScript works them out (history's tsserver plugin,\n`_history.fileRename`), once the move's made and TypeScript can say, as VS Code's own TypeScript support does: worked out\nbefore it, a slow start lost them (VS Code waits a minute for what a move waits on, then moves without it). And what an agent\nasks, each the same thing a person does:\n\n- `code.references` { path, line, name }: Find All References on the name on that line, each place's file, line, column and\ntext, its declaration included.\n- `code.rename` { path, line, name, to }: Rename Symbol, everywhere TypeScript renames it, every file saved.\n- `code.move` { from, to }: the Explorer's rename, answered once its imports are right as above, every file it touched saved.\n\nThe projects are told of files made since first (`_history.files`), then the file asked its symbols, so the TypeScript server\nholds its project: in the browser it isn't told of files made, and opening a document doesn't hand it over.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:17:43.019Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:17:43.019Z"}
{"id":"8cb40567-a792-48ba-8f2b-791802c3cbc0","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"44dec6daabd01df0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/code-refactor.ts","baseline":{"blob":"57dba609ebe21d822745fd3440d30800508072df","start":6851,"end":6884},"shape":{"type":"MemberExpression","atoms":["vscode",".","workspace",".","onDidRenameFiles"]},"context":{"before":"eb384a871dbd5b38","after":"d118393aca4aecbe"}},"payload":{"text":"The Explorer's moves and renames, and anything else's (an extension's edit, code.move): their imports kept right.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:17:21.052Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:17:21.052Z"}
